WEBVTT

00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:19.932
Gasterly Ghosts by Gina D.B.

00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:21.013
Clement.

00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:33.186
Chapter 1 What is a Ghost?

00:00:33.247 --> 00:00:50.652
Centuries ago, people talked about ghosts, spirits and spooks and they still talk about them today.

00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:56.304
But no one knows exactly what a ghost is.

00:00:56.364 --> 00:01:05.038
Certain scientists and psychic experts study ghosts and haunted places.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:13.236
They try to understand supernatural events of the past and present.

00:01:13.296 --> 00:01:20.518
Psychic experts use complex machines to discover ghosts.

00:01:20.578 --> 00:01:25.088
Others try to photograph ghosts.

00:01:25.148 --> 00:01:33.204
Sometimes ghosts appear in photographs and no one can explain why.

00:01:33.264 --> 00:01:40.648
Today, several important universities have a parapsychology department.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:51.230
In these departments, experts study the supernatural and try to find an answer to old questions.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:55.061
So, what is a ghost?

00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:59.032
The most common explanation is this.

00:01:59.092 --> 00:02:02.638
Ghosts are spirits of the dead.

00:02:02.698 --> 00:02:07.797
Their death was a tragic or terrible one.

00:02:07.857 --> 00:02:11.350
They haunt the place where they died.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:20.968
It can be a house, a castle, a theatre, a forest, a road or a ship.

00:02:21.028 --> 00:02:25.012
They cannot rest in peace.

00:02:25.072 --> 00:02:28.726
Do ghosts really exist?

00:02:28.785 --> 00:02:31.290
What do you think?

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:37.823
Read this book carefully and become a ghost investigator.

00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:49.525
Fill in the phantom file with your opinion after each case and then decide.

00:02:49.585 --> 00:03:08.424
Chapter 2 The Horror of Barclay Square There are many ghosts in the city of London There are haunted houses, theatres, streets and pubs.

00:03:08.484 --> 00:03:14.669
One of the most evil ghosts is the one at Barclay Square.

00:03:14.729 --> 00:03:24.076
Between 1870 and 1900, no one wanted to live at 50 Barclay Square.

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:30.365
There were footsteps at night and macabre appearances.

00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:37.013
One particular room in the house was especially dangerous.

00:03:37.073 --> 00:03:46.630
In 1870, a brave young man decided to sleep in the haunted room for one night.

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:50.592
Ghosts don't scare me, he said.

00:03:50.652 --> 00:03:54.856
The next morning, he was dead.

00:03:54.916 --> 00:03:59.562
His body was in the middle of the evil room.

00:03:59.622 --> 00:04:05.240
A year later, a young girl slept in the haunted room.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:12.292
That night, she saw or heard something horrible.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:16.835
The next morning, she was mad.

00:04:16.894 --> 00:04:24.028
She could not speak about her horrifying experience to anyone.

00:04:24.088 --> 00:04:29.046
Lord Littleton was an English Lord.

00:04:29.106 --> 00:04:31.593
I don't believe in ghosts.

00:04:31.653 --> 00:04:33.493
He told his friends.

00:04:33.553 --> 00:04:38.254
I will sleep in that house, and nothing will happen to me.

00:04:38.314 --> 00:04:46.678
During the night, the people in the next house heard a gunshot.

00:04:46.737 --> 00:04:55.180
The next morning, Lord Littleton was terrified and told them.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.141
Something came into the room from that corner.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:03.082
It was slimy and had an evil smell.

00:05:03.142 --> 00:05:07.403
I fired my gun at it, and the ghost disappeared.

00:05:07.463 --> 00:05:09.054
It was horrible.

00:05:09.114 --> 00:05:11.744
I cannot describe it.

00:05:11.804 --> 00:05:16.936
That house is haunted by a ghastly spirit.

00:05:16.996 --> 00:05:22.588
A year later, a maid was cleaning the haunted room.

00:05:22.648 --> 00:05:26.788
She did not know about the evil ghost.

00:05:26.848 --> 00:05:37.182
At midnight, horrible cries came from the haunted room.

00:05:37.242 --> 00:05:42.655
The people in the house ran upstairs.

00:05:42.715 --> 00:05:49.249
They found the poor maid on the floor in convulsions.

00:05:49.308 --> 00:05:54.924
Her terrified eyes stared at a corner of the room.

00:05:54.984 --> 00:06:00.819
It was the same corner Lord Littleton indicated.

00:06:00.879 --> 00:06:04.580
The maid refused to speak.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:13.394
Her only words were, What I saw was too horrible to describe.

00:06:13.454 --> 00:06:20.100
The next morning she died at St George's Hospital.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:28.839
The story of the two sailors is perhaps the most famous of all.

00:06:28.899 --> 00:06:34.292
In 1875, two sailors arrived in London.

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:37.874
They wanted to work on a ship.

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:42.758
They had no money and nowhere to sleep.

00:06:42.818 --> 00:06:48.102
They walked around London and came to Barclay Square.

00:06:48.162 --> 00:06:49.458
Look!

00:06:49.518 --> 00:06:51.493
said the younger sailor.

00:06:51.553 --> 00:06:53.424
There's an empty house.

00:06:53.484 --> 00:06:55.374
We can sleep there.

00:06:55.434 --> 00:07:00.075
The sailors entered the dark empty house.

00:07:00.135 --> 00:07:03.076
They went up the stairs.

00:07:03.136 --> 00:07:06.006
The older sailor said...

00:07:06.066 --> 00:07:09.457
This house is cold and dark.

00:07:09.517 --> 00:07:11.007
I don't like it.

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:12.648
It scares me.

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:14.348
Don't be silly.

00:07:14.408 --> 00:07:16.538
Said the younger sailor.

00:07:16.598 --> 00:07:18.429
We have nowhere to sleep.

00:07:18.489 --> 00:07:20.352
I'd stay here.

00:07:20.412 --> 00:07:24.236
They slept in the haunted bedroom.

00:07:24.296 --> 00:07:28.878
In the middle of the night, they both woke up.

00:07:28.938 --> 00:07:30.488
Listen.

00:07:30.548 --> 00:07:32.459
Said the younger one.

00:07:32.519 --> 00:07:35.100
There's someone downstairs.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.391
Can you hear the noise?

00:07:37.451 --> 00:07:38.492
Yes.

00:07:38.552 --> 00:07:40.012
Said the other.

00:07:40.072 --> 00:07:42.193
I can hear footsteps.

00:07:42.253 --> 00:07:43.794
Oh no.

00:07:43.854 --> 00:07:47.532
The footsteps are coming upstairs.

00:07:47.592 --> 00:07:52.980
At that moment, the door opened slowly.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.020
A big, dark figure came in.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.942
The older sailor was terrified.

00:08:01.002 --> 00:08:03.502
He could not move.

00:08:03.562 --> 00:08:09.414
He just sat and looked at the horrible thing.

00:08:09.474 --> 00:08:18.012
The younger sailor ran out of the room, down the stairs and out of the house.

00:08:18.072 --> 00:08:21.960
In the street, he found a policeman.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:28.545
They returned to the house, but the sailor was too frightened to enter.

00:08:28.605 --> 00:08:33.048
The policeman went upstairs alone.

00:08:33.109 --> 00:08:35.470
Is anyone here?

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.312
He cried.

00:08:37.372 --> 00:08:43.116
There was no answer, and he found no one.

00:08:43.177 --> 00:08:47.767
There was an evil smell on the stairs.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:53.906
He looked everywhere, but he couldn't find the older sailor.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:57.828
Then he looked out of the window.

00:08:57.887 --> 00:09:02.579
The older sailor was lying in the garden.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.361
He was dead.

00:09:05.421 --> 00:09:10.444
Did something push him out of the window?

00:09:10.504 --> 00:09:15.055
Or did he jump out of the window in terror?

00:09:15.116 --> 00:09:20.452
We will never know.

00:09:20.512 --> 00:09:25.128
Listening exercise.

00:09:25.188 --> 00:09:33.259
Chapter 2 Listen to the conversation between the two sailors.

00:09:33.319 --> 00:09:42.171
For each question, choose the correct answer A, B or C.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:45.781
What a rainy evening.

00:09:45.841 --> 00:09:49.524
I'm wet and I'm tired of walking.

00:09:49.584 --> 00:09:51.338
You're right.

00:09:51.398 --> 00:09:54.389
I'm cold and very hungry.

00:09:54.449 --> 00:09:57.070
I'm very hungry too.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.271
It's half past six.

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:03.132
Look, there's a small bakery near the church.

00:10:03.192 --> 00:10:04.273
Yes.

00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:06.754
Let's go and see.

00:10:06.815 --> 00:10:11.662
I want to buy that big apple pie in the window.

00:10:11.722 --> 00:10:15.319
And I want some chocolate biscuits.

00:10:15.379 --> 00:10:20.811
Then we can go to the yellow duck tavern and have a hot cup of tea.

00:10:20.871 --> 00:10:22.912
What a good idea!

00:10:22.972 --> 00:10:27.164
It's always warm at the yellow duck tavern.

00:10:27.224 --> 00:10:30.294
Then we must find a place to sleep.

00:10:30.354 --> 00:10:35.366
Yes, but let's go to the barkly bakery first.

00:10:35.426 --> 00:10:39.310
I'm hungry.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:54.722
Chapter 3 Glam's Castle and its Ghosts Scotland is famous for its haunted castles and its ghosts.

00:10:54.782 --> 00:11:02.236
Glam's Castle has a long history of violent murders and ghosts.

00:11:02.296 --> 00:11:11.931
It is a big castle with more than 100 rooms and many secret hiding places.

00:11:11.991 --> 00:11:17.934
The castle also hides terrible secrets.

00:11:17.994 --> 00:11:24.142
During the Middle Ages, there was a battle near the castle.

00:11:24.202 --> 00:11:28.706
After the battle, some men came to the castle.

00:11:28.766 --> 00:11:32.830
They were afraid and in danger.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.121
Excuse us, sir.

00:11:35.181 --> 00:11:36.782
We are in danger.

00:11:36.842 --> 00:11:38.713
The enemy is following us.

00:11:38.773 --> 00:11:41.874
Can we stay at your castle for a few days?

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.716
They said.

00:11:43.776 --> 00:11:48.498
The Earl of Glam's smiled and said...

00:11:48.558 --> 00:11:50.329
Follow me.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.852
You can hide in a secret room.

00:11:53.912 --> 00:11:57.454
The men were happy and said...

00:11:57.514 --> 00:11:58.714
Thank you, sir.

00:11:58.774 --> 00:12:01.008
You are very kind.

00:12:01.068 --> 00:12:08.286
The Earl of Glam's looked at the men, but did not answer.

00:12:08.346 --> 00:12:11.837
He took them to a secret room.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:15.639
Enter, and don't make any noise.

00:12:15.699 --> 00:12:17.470
He said.

00:12:17.531 --> 00:12:20.281
The men entered.

00:12:20.342 --> 00:12:29.167
The Earl locked the door and put the key in his pocket.

00:12:29.227 --> 00:12:33.980
He never opened that door again.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:42.115
Many years later, Lord Strathmore opened that door and fainted.

00:12:42.175 --> 00:12:47.298
He found a room full of skeletons.

00:12:47.358 --> 00:12:53.431
Visitors to the castle often hear strange noises in that room.

00:12:53.492 --> 00:12:58.082
They hear knocks at the door.

00:12:58.142 --> 00:13:04.974
Perhaps the ghosts of the men want to get out.

00:13:05.034 --> 00:13:10.696
The grey lady is another ghost of Glam's castle.

00:13:10.757 --> 00:13:18.479
Lady Janet Glam's lived during the reign of King James V of Scotland.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:24.948
King James was a cruel man and did not like Janet.

00:13:25.008 --> 00:13:28.636
Lady Janet Douglas Glams is a witch.

00:13:28.696 --> 00:13:31.128
She tried to poison me.

00:13:31.188 --> 00:13:34.181
He said to his court.

00:13:34.241 --> 00:13:38.534
No, that is not true.

00:13:38.594 --> 00:13:41.328
Cried Lady Janet.

00:13:41.388 --> 00:13:43.680
I am not a witch.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:46.810
I am innocent.

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:57.402
The king sent poor Lady Janet to prison for many years, and she was very unhappy.

00:13:57.462 --> 00:14:05.015
Then, in 1537, the king's men burned her.

00:14:05.075 --> 00:14:10.536
Her ghost haunts the clock tower of Glam's castle.

00:14:10.596 --> 00:14:15.317
People say her ghost is transparent.

00:14:15.377 --> 00:14:22.002
and there is a strange red light around her head.

00:14:22.062 --> 00:14:29.848
At the beginning of the 1800s, the Earl of Strathmore had a son.

00:14:29.908 --> 00:14:33.280
The baby was deformed.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:38.866
The parents hid the baby in a secret room.

00:14:38.926 --> 00:14:44.952
Only the parents and the nurse knew about the baby.

00:14:45.012 --> 00:14:51.738
The boy grew up but he always stayed in the secret room.

00:14:51.798 --> 00:14:56.851
No one knew the terrible secret.

00:14:56.911 --> 00:15:02.214
One day a workman went to repair the roof.

00:15:02.274 --> 00:15:10.246
From the roof he saw the window of the secret room and looked inside.

00:15:10.306 --> 00:15:15.026
He was terrified and began to shout.

00:15:15.086 --> 00:15:18.637
There's a strange creature in that room!

00:15:18.697 --> 00:15:21.917
What people say is true!

00:15:21.977 --> 00:15:25.318
The Earl heard him and said...

00:15:25.378 --> 00:15:27.098
Listen carefully.

00:15:27.158 --> 00:15:29.559
You saw nothing.

00:15:29.619 --> 00:15:32.060
But sir, I did!

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.959
I saw a...

00:15:34.019 --> 00:15:38.309
You saw no one and heard nothing.

00:15:38.369 --> 00:15:40.379
Do you understand?

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:44.910
I am sending you and your family away from Scotland.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.360
I don't want to go away, sir.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.881
Take your family and go to Australia.

00:15:50.941 --> 00:15:52.822
Here is lots of money.

00:15:52.882 --> 00:15:54.392
Now go.

00:15:54.452 --> 00:16:01.048
The next day, the workman and his family left Scotland.

00:16:01.108 --> 00:16:05.906
The creature died when he was very old.

00:16:05.966 --> 00:16:12.385
Perhaps his skeleton is still in the secret room.

00:16:12.445 --> 00:16:20.934
Today people at the castle can hear a child crying at night.

00:16:20.994 --> 00:16:37.894
Others say that the ghost of a strange creature walks around the castle and makes unusual noises.

00:16:37.954 --> 00:16:58.390
Chapter 4 – Bali A haunted village Bali is a small village about 100 km northeast of London.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:04.345
It has a church, a rectory and a few houses.

00:17:04.406 --> 00:17:10.766
It also has more ghosts than any other village in England.

00:17:10.826 --> 00:17:15.773
In 1863, Reverend Henry D.

00:17:15.833 --> 00:17:19.054
Bull built the Bawley Rectory.

00:17:19.114 --> 00:17:30.298
When he died in 1892, his son became minister and lived in the rectory with his wife and daughters.

00:17:30.358 --> 00:17:40.337
On the 28th of July 1900, Reverend Bull heard a noise outside the rectory.

00:17:40.398 --> 00:17:45.118
He opened the door and saw his daughters.

00:17:45.178 --> 00:17:49.040
They were very frightened.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:52.192
We saw Ghost.

00:17:52.252 --> 00:17:54.212
They cried.

00:17:54.272 --> 00:17:57.744
It was a nun, a young nun.

00:17:57.804 --> 00:18:01.707
She was silent and very sad.

00:18:01.767 --> 00:18:04.958
She walked in front of us.

00:18:05.019 --> 00:18:07.160
Where is the Ghost now?

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:09.884
asked Reverend Bull.

00:18:09.944 --> 00:18:15.397
It appeared, said one of the girls.

00:18:15.458 --> 00:18:31.612
Some people did not believe the girls, but a doctor and a teacher saw the same nun on the same day, the 28th of July, a few years later.

00:18:31.673 --> 00:18:38.273
On the 28th of July 1972, a group of scientists saw her too.

00:18:38.333 --> 00:18:45.904
The nun was not the only ghost of Bawley Rectory.

00:18:45.964 --> 00:18:55.866
There was also a headless man, a phantom coach with two horses and others.

00:18:55.926 --> 00:19:15.971
Other bizarre happenings at Bawley included organ music playing in the empty church, lights that went on and off, furniture that moved and stones that fell from the sky.

00:19:16.031 --> 00:19:23.967
Reverend Guy Smith arrived at Bawley Rectory in 1928.

00:19:24.027 --> 00:19:31.584
He and his wife didn't like the noises and the other strange events.

00:19:31.644 --> 00:19:34.676
I don't believe in ghosts.

00:19:34.736 --> 00:19:37.162
It's all a lot of nonsense.

00:19:37.222 --> 00:19:42.620
but I want to understand what is happening," said Reverend Smith.

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:48.132
So he called Harry Price to investigate.

00:19:48.192 --> 00:19:52.974
Price was a famous psychic expert.

00:19:53.034 --> 00:20:00.294
He arrived at Bali with several assistants and started investigating.

00:20:00.354 --> 00:20:14.242
On the 10th of June 1929, there was a sensational newspaper article in the Daily Mirror about the ghostly figures at Bawley.

00:20:14.302 --> 00:20:20.384
Hundreds of curious visitors came to Bawley Rectory.

00:20:20.444 --> 00:20:24.244
They wanted to see the ghosts.

00:20:24.304 --> 00:20:29.674
Reverend Smith did not like all these visitors.

00:20:29.734 --> 00:20:37.406
He soon left, but Harry Price continued investigating.

00:20:37.466 --> 00:20:42.648
He wrote books about the rectory and its ghosts.

00:20:42.708 --> 00:20:49.282
Soon, Reverend Forrester and his family arrived at Bawley.

00:20:49.342 --> 00:20:56.025
He and his family had the same problems as the other Revrons.

00:20:56.085 --> 00:21:00.898
He kept a diary of the bizarre events.

00:21:00.958 --> 00:21:09.102
During this time, mysterious messages appeared on the walls of the Rectory.

00:21:09.163 --> 00:21:14.496
They were written to the Reverend's wife, Marianne.

00:21:14.556 --> 00:21:18.338
Who wrote these messages?

00:21:18.398 --> 00:21:20.770
Was it a ghost?

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:24.702
Or was it Mrs. Feuster?

00:21:24.762 --> 00:21:36.034
After five years and about 2,000 ghostly appearances, Reverend Forrester left Bawley.

00:21:36.094 --> 00:21:40.588
He was the last Reverend at Bawley Rectory.

00:21:40.648 --> 00:21:44.762
No one wanted to live there.

00:21:44.822 --> 00:21:52.242
On the 27th of February 1939, a big fire destroyed the Rectory.

00:21:52.302 --> 00:22:05.431
After the fire, workmen found a woman's skull in the ground and several religious symbols.

00:22:05.491 --> 00:22:12.002
People said the ghosts moved to the church after the fire.

00:22:12.062 --> 00:22:15.923
But why is Bawley haunted?

00:22:15.983 --> 00:22:20.964
Why does the nun appear to many people in the village?

00:22:21.024 --> 00:22:24.508
Who are the other ghosts?

00:22:24.568 --> 00:22:32.814
A legend says the rectory was built on the ruins of a medieval monastery.

00:22:32.875 --> 00:22:37.078
Near the monastery, there was a convent.

00:22:37.138 --> 00:22:42.661
A monk fell in love with a young nun at the convent.

00:22:42.721 --> 00:22:52.150
On the night of the 28th of July, they decided to escape together in a coach.

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:58.026
But the nuns of the convent discovered their plan.

00:22:58.086 --> 00:23:01.248
They were very angry.

00:23:01.308 --> 00:23:09.442
They shut the young nun in a small room and she starved to death.

00:23:09.502 --> 00:23:13.596
The monk was beheaded.

00:23:13.656 --> 00:23:25.262
During the 1960s, a psychic expert, called Jeffrey Crum Hollingsworth, was interested in Borley.

00:23:25.322 --> 00:23:32.374
He and his assistant, Roy Potter, spent a lot of time there.

00:23:32.434 --> 00:23:36.906
This is what Crum Hollingsworth said.

00:23:36.966 --> 00:23:42.114
One summer night, I saw the nun walking across the garden.

00:23:42.174 --> 00:23:46.214
I called Roy Potter and he saw her too.

00:23:46.274 --> 00:23:49.496
She was about four metres from us.

00:23:49.556 --> 00:23:53.489
Then she disappeared into a wall.

00:23:53.549 --> 00:24:02.266
Crume Hollingsworth and Potter studied the bizarre events at Bali for many years.

00:24:02.326 --> 00:24:04.958
Their conclusion?

00:24:05.019 --> 00:24:10.346
Bali is haunted.

00:24:10.406 --> 00:24:24.183
Chapter 5 Royal Ghosts Today the Tower of London is a popular tourist attraction.

00:24:24.243 --> 00:24:28.604
Millions of people visit it every year.

00:24:28.664 --> 00:24:34.245
Do they know the tower is haunted by royal ghosts?

00:24:34.305 --> 00:24:43.674
William the Conqueror wanted a castle and a prison and built the Tower of London in 1078.

00:24:43.734 --> 00:24:53.950
The tower has a ghastly history of torches, murders and executions.

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:59.594
Anbulin is a very active royal ghost.

00:24:59.654 --> 00:25:04.932
In 1533, she became King Henry VIII's second wife.

00:25:04.992 --> 00:25:13.531
But Henry soon got tired of her because she did not give him a son.

00:25:13.591 --> 00:25:20.273
In 1536 Henry decided to marry another woman.

00:25:20.333 --> 00:25:27.125
He accused Anne Bullen of treason and put her in the Tower of London.

00:25:27.185 --> 00:25:33.779
She was beheaded on Tower Green in May 1536.

00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:39.516
Her ghost is white and transparent.

00:25:39.576 --> 00:25:46.702
She haunts tower green, the white tower and the church in the tower.

00:25:46.762 --> 00:25:50.906
Sometimes she appears with her head.

00:25:50.966 --> 00:25:56.703
At other times she holds her head in her hand.

00:25:56.763 --> 00:26:11.917
The ghosts of Henry's other unlucky wives, Catherine Howard and Jane Seymour, haunt Hampton Court Palace just outside London.

00:26:11.977 --> 00:26:19.714
In 1972, a nine-year-old girl visited the Tower of London with her father.

00:26:19.774 --> 00:26:28.418
The tourist guide said, Anne Berlin and other royal prisoners were beheaded on Tower Green.

00:26:28.478 --> 00:26:33.814
The executioner used a big axe to cut off their heads.

00:26:33.874 --> 00:26:35.655
That's not true.

00:26:35.675 --> 00:26:39.608
I saw Anne Berlin a minute ago.

00:26:39.668 --> 00:26:45.063
But the executioner did not use an axe because Anne Berlin was a queen.

00:26:45.083 --> 00:26:50.425
He used a special sword from France.

00:26:50.485 --> 00:26:54.394
The other visitors were surprised.

00:26:54.454 --> 00:26:57.346
The little girl was right.

00:26:57.406 --> 00:26:59.648
How do you know this?

00:26:59.708 --> 00:27:02.110
asked her father.

00:27:02.170 --> 00:27:10.576
I saw the whole execution on Tower Green a few minutes ago, she said.

00:27:10.636 --> 00:27:17.760
Perhaps the most famous ghosts of the Tower are the two princes.

00:27:17.820 --> 00:27:21.395
They were heirs to the English throne.

00:27:21.455 --> 00:27:34.156
When Edward V became King of England in 1483, he was only 12 years old and his brother Richard was 10.

00:27:34.216 --> 00:27:39.590
Their uncle, Richard, wanted to be King of England.

00:27:39.650 --> 00:27:45.824
He took the princes to the tower and soon they disappeared.

00:27:45.884 --> 00:27:49.496
People began asking questions.

00:27:49.557 --> 00:27:51.824
Where is young King Edward?

00:27:51.884 --> 00:27:53.940
Where is his brother?

00:27:54.000 --> 00:28:00.876
People said that Richard was responsible for the murder of the princes.

00:28:00.936 --> 00:28:08.862
Then one night, a soldier saw two children at the bottom of the stairs.

00:28:08.922 --> 00:28:13.355
They had long, white night clothes.

00:28:13.415 --> 00:28:17.548
They looked at the soldier silently.

00:28:17.608 --> 00:28:21.884
They were very sad and frightened.

00:28:21.944 --> 00:28:25.820
Suddenly, they disappeared.

00:28:25.880 --> 00:28:29.382
Then the soldier understood.

00:28:29.442 --> 00:28:34.546
The children were the ghosts of the two princes.

00:28:34.606 --> 00:28:43.863
Many people saw the two ghosts at the bottom of the stairs, and people still see them now.

00:28:43.923 --> 00:28:52.727
In 1647, workmen found the skeletons of two children under the stairs.

00:28:52.787 --> 00:28:57.148
The skeletons were buried immediately.

00:28:57.208 --> 00:29:05.776
On windy nights, the ghosts of the sad princes still haunt the Tower of London.

00:29:05.836 --> 00:29:13.772
The Tower is a very spooky place at night.

00:29:13.832 --> 00:29:25.356
Listening exercise, Chapter 5 The two princes are in the Tower of London.

00:29:25.416 --> 00:29:31.567
Listen to what they say and then complete the form.

00:29:31.628 --> 00:29:34.798
I don't like the Tower of London.

00:29:34.858 --> 00:29:37.429
Our room is small and cold.

00:29:37.489 --> 00:29:41.050
Yes, and there is only one window.

00:29:41.110 --> 00:29:47.994
And we haven't got much furniture, only a table, a chair and a bed.

00:29:48.054 --> 00:29:53.370
I'm bored because we haven't got any toys to play with.

00:29:53.430 --> 00:29:58.024
I'm always hungry because we only get one meal a day.

00:29:58.084 --> 00:29:59.776
What a meal.

00:29:59.836 --> 00:30:03.098
We have some bread and some milk.

00:30:03.158 --> 00:30:06.630
And the three guards are very unfriendly.

00:30:06.691 --> 00:30:09.402
What a terrible place.

00:30:09.462 --> 00:30:13.504
I want to go home.

00:30:13.564 --> 00:30:20.698
Chapter 6, American Spooks.

00:30:20.759 --> 00:30:30.378
Ghosts, spooks, poltergeists, and phantoms are part of America's past and present.

00:30:30.438 --> 00:30:40.234
Halloween is the festivity of ghosts and the supernatural, and as you know, it is celebrated on October 31st.

00:30:40.294 --> 00:30:49.936
The Winchester Mystery House in San Jose, California is the spookiest American monument to ghosts.

00:30:49.996 --> 00:30:57.040
It is a famous tourist attraction, and people say that mysterious spooks live there.

00:30:57.100 --> 00:31:01.852
Sarah Winchester was part of the rich Winchester family.

00:31:01.912 --> 00:31:06.084
The family made Winchester rifles in the 1800s.

00:31:06.144 --> 00:31:12.487
During the 19th century, these rifles killed many people.

00:31:12.547 --> 00:31:18.721
When Sarah Winchester's husband and baby daughter died, she was very unhappy.

00:31:18.782 --> 00:31:22.054
Strange things were happening to her.

00:31:22.115 --> 00:31:26.728
She went to a psychic expert and asked for help.

00:31:26.788 --> 00:31:34.394
The expert told her, The spirits of the people killed by a Winchester rifle are angry with you.

00:31:34.454 --> 00:31:36.502
They want revenge.

00:31:36.562 --> 00:31:40.132
What can I do, Mrs. Winchester asked?

00:31:40.192 --> 00:31:42.064
The expert answered.

00:31:42.124 --> 00:31:45.706
The spirits want you to build a big home for them.

00:31:45.766 --> 00:31:48.668
You must follow all their instructions.

00:31:48.728 --> 00:31:50.940
And you cannot rest.

00:31:51.000 --> 00:31:53.962
You must work seven days a week.

00:31:54.022 --> 00:31:58.264
Mrs. Winchester bought a house in the country.

00:31:58.324 --> 00:32:03.506
For 38 years, she built a home for ghosts.

00:32:03.566 --> 00:32:07.536
She and the workmen worked seven days a week.

00:32:07.596 --> 00:32:17.614
She lived in the haunted house, and every evening she wore a long blue dress and had dinner and secret meetings with the ghost.

00:32:17.674 --> 00:32:22.128
They gave her instructions for building the strange house.

00:32:22.188 --> 00:32:26.718
Every night she slept in a different bedroom.

00:32:26.779 --> 00:32:36.110
Today, the Winchester Mystery House has 160 rooms and is similar to a maze.

00:32:36.170 --> 00:32:47.095
There are stairs that go nowhere, doors that open onto walls, and a window in the floor.

00:32:47.115 --> 00:32:56.302
13 was a favorite number of the ghosts because there are 13 bathrooms and all the stairs have 13 steps.

00:32:56.362 --> 00:33:04.346
Nathaniel Hawthorne was born in Salem, Massachusetts in 1804.

00:33:04.406 --> 00:33:07.907
He was a famous American writer.

00:33:07.967 --> 00:33:13.458
His grandfather was a judge at the Salem witch hangings.

00:33:13.518 --> 00:33:20.030
He was very interested in ghosts, evil spirits, and demons.

00:33:20.090 --> 00:33:33.354
Every evening after work, Hawthorne went to the Athenium Library to read the newspaper Reverend Harris went to the Athenium Library, too.

00:33:33.414 --> 00:33:36.845
He was an old minister of the church.

00:33:36.905 --> 00:33:45.327
Hawthorne saw Reverend Harris every evening for many years, but they were not friends.

00:33:45.387 --> 00:33:52.438
One evening, a friend of Hawthorne said, Reverend Harris died last week.

00:33:52.499 --> 00:33:53.999
What?

00:33:54.059 --> 00:33:55.629
Are you sure?

00:33:55.689 --> 00:33:57.150
Hawthorne asked.

00:33:57.210 --> 00:33:58.610
Yes, of course.

00:33:58.670 --> 00:34:01.682
His friend answered and went away.

00:34:01.742 --> 00:34:04.204
How is that possible?

00:34:04.264 --> 00:34:08.636
I saw Reverend Harris at the library this evening and all last week.

00:34:08.696 --> 00:34:10.597
Hawthorne thought?

00:34:10.657 --> 00:34:16.181
For many weeks Hawthorne saw Reverend Harris at the library.

00:34:16.242 --> 00:34:21.084
He sat in his usual chair and read the newspaper.

00:34:21.144 --> 00:34:25.768
But the other people at the library could not see him.

00:34:25.828 --> 00:34:29.458
Hawthorne said nothing to the others.

00:34:29.518 --> 00:34:32.878
He was afraid to talk to the Ghost.

00:34:32.939 --> 00:34:36.031
He was also afraid to touch it.

00:34:36.091 --> 00:34:41.315
After about a month, the Ghost started looking at him.

00:34:41.375 --> 00:34:45.469
Why is Reverend Harris's Ghost looking at me?

00:34:45.529 --> 00:34:48.541
Perhaps he wants to say something.

00:34:48.601 --> 00:34:50.433
Hawthorne thought.

00:34:50.493 --> 00:34:52.725
He was confused.

00:34:52.785 --> 00:34:56.849
He saw the Ghost and did not know what to do.

00:34:56.909 --> 00:35:02.344
One evening, he went to the library and Reverend Harris's chair was empty.

00:35:02.364 --> 00:35:06.848
Hawthorne never saw the ghost again.

00:35:06.908 --> 00:35:09.370
For years, he thought.

00:35:09.430 --> 00:35:12.833
Why did I see Reverend Harris's ghost?

00:35:12.893 --> 00:35:15.795
Why didn't the other people see him?

00:35:15.856 --> 00:35:25.214
Hawthorne thought about Reverend Harris's ghost for a long time, but he was never able to solve the mystery.

00:35:25.274 --> 00:35:31.758
The White House in Washington DC is also a haunted house.

00:35:31.818 --> 00:35:36.980
The ghost of assassinated American presidents haunted.

00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:41.801
Abraham Lincoln's ghost is the most famous.

00:35:41.861 --> 00:35:48.423
Lincoln was president of the United States during the American Civil War.

00:35:48.483 --> 00:35:54.152
Many Americans loved him, but he had dangerous enemies too.

00:35:54.212 --> 00:36:00.621
He stopped slavery in America, but the Southern states did not agree with this.

00:36:00.682 --> 00:36:09.123
On the 5th of April 1865, Abraham Lincoln had a very bad dream.

00:36:09.184 --> 00:36:15.625
He was at the White House and he heard people crying in the next room.

00:36:15.685 --> 00:36:19.696
He got up and went to the East Room.

00:36:19.756 --> 00:36:23.565
He saw a coffin in the middle of the room.

00:36:23.625 --> 00:36:26.873
Many people walked by the coffin.

00:36:26.934 --> 00:36:29.004
Who was inside the coffin?

00:36:29.064 --> 00:36:30.874
He asked a man.

00:36:30.934 --> 00:36:33.935
The President of the United States, sir.

00:36:33.995 --> 00:36:36.046
An assassin killed him.

00:36:36.106 --> 00:36:36.946
What?

00:36:37.006 --> 00:36:38.286
Said Lincoln.

00:36:38.346 --> 00:36:43.217
He looked inside the coffin and saw his own body.

00:36:43.277 --> 00:36:45.147
He was dead.

00:36:45.208 --> 00:36:47.408
He suddenly woke up.

00:36:47.468 --> 00:36:50.428
He was very scared about this dream.

00:36:50.488 --> 00:36:53.690
He told his wife and friends.

00:36:53.750 --> 00:37:01.104
On the 15th of April 1865, Lincoln and his wife went to the theater.

00:37:01.164 --> 00:37:05.436
He wanted to relax after a long day.

00:37:05.496 --> 00:37:13.761
At the end of the performance, John Wilkes Booth shot the President in the back of the head.

00:37:13.822 --> 00:37:18.404
The President of the United States was dead.

00:37:18.464 --> 00:37:25.574
was Lincoln's dream a coincidence, or did he have supernatural powers?

00:37:25.634 --> 00:37:34.547
In the 1920s, President Coolidge's wife saw Lincoln's face at the window of the Oval Office.

00:37:34.607 --> 00:37:37.998
He was very sad.

00:37:38.058 --> 00:37:45.648
In the 1930s, Queen Wilhelmina of the Netherlands was a guest at the White House.

00:37:45.708 --> 00:37:50.066
One evening she heard a knock at the door.

00:37:50.126 --> 00:37:54.448
She opened it and saw Lincoln's ghost.

00:37:54.508 --> 00:37:58.390
He looked at her and then walked away.

00:37:58.450 --> 00:38:04.742
In the 1980s, President Reagan's daughter saw Lincoln's ghost too.

00:38:04.802 --> 00:38:15.876
Today, people at the White House still see his ghost in the East Room, in the Oval Office and in the halls.

00:38:15.937 --> 00:38:22.260
Listening exercise, chapter six.

00:38:22.320 --> 00:38:26.791
Mike and Sue are at the Winchester Mystery House.

00:38:26.851 --> 00:38:29.972
Listen to their conversation.

00:38:30.032 --> 00:38:34.754
Where can Mike and Sue do the following things?

00:38:34.814 --> 00:38:42.156
For questions one through five, write a letter A through F in the correct box.

00:38:42.216 --> 00:38:46.439
Let's go to the ticket office and get some tickets.

00:38:46.499 --> 00:38:47.840
Good idea.

00:38:47.900 --> 00:38:49.832
What do you want to see first?

00:38:49.892 --> 00:38:55.584
I want to see the old rifles at the Winchester Firearms Museum.

00:38:55.644 --> 00:38:58.506
Where can we buy some postcards?

00:38:58.566 --> 00:39:00.547
At the gift shop.

00:39:00.607 --> 00:39:03.068
I'm hungry and thirsty.

00:39:03.128 --> 00:39:04.599
So am I.

00:39:04.659 --> 00:39:08.371
Let's have lunch at the Winchester Cafe.

00:39:08.431 --> 00:39:11.292
What time does the Mystery House close?

00:39:11.352 --> 00:39:16.901
Let's ask the Information Office.

00:39:16.961 --> 00:39:32.595
Chapter 7 Spanish Spirits Maria Juan and Miguel Pereira lived in the village of Belmez in southern Spain.

00:39:32.655 --> 00:39:35.116
They were farmers.

00:39:35.176 --> 00:39:41.424
On 23 August 1971, Maria Pereira was in the kitchen of her home.

00:39:41.484 --> 00:39:50.313
Suddenly, she saw an image of a human face on the kitchen floor.

00:39:50.374 --> 00:39:56.627
She tried to wash the floor, but the face did not go away.

00:39:56.688 --> 00:39:59.920
It became more visible.

00:39:59.980 --> 00:40:05.994
It was the sad face of a man with big eyes.

00:40:06.054 --> 00:40:09.486
One, come quickly.

00:40:09.546 --> 00:40:13.629
There is something strange on the kitchen floor.

00:40:13.689 --> 00:40:16.062
Maria cried.

00:40:16.122 --> 00:40:20.836
Her husband came quickly and looked at the floor.

00:40:20.896 --> 00:40:23.458
He was terrified.

00:40:23.518 --> 00:40:25.170
Oh no!

00:40:25.230 --> 00:40:26.890
What is this?

00:40:26.950 --> 00:40:29.072
A human face!

00:40:29.132 --> 00:40:30.884
Call Miguel!

00:40:30.944 --> 00:40:39.462
One said, their son Miguel looked at the floor and said, What's happening?

00:40:39.522 --> 00:40:41.617
This is Macabre.

00:40:41.677 --> 00:40:47.352
Miguel took a hammer and destroyed part of the floor.

00:40:47.412 --> 00:40:57.764
But soon after another face appeared and then another, Miguel destroyed another part of the floor.

00:40:57.824 --> 00:41:03.206
But after a few days other faces appeared.

00:41:03.266 --> 00:41:10.160
There were faces of men, women and children of different ages.

00:41:10.220 --> 00:41:15.384
Sometimes small crosses appeared too.

00:41:15.444 --> 00:41:20.185
At other times parts of the body were visible.

00:41:20.245 --> 00:41:23.946
A woman's hand with a flower.

00:41:24.006 --> 00:41:30.748
Soon everyone in Belmez knew about the mysterious faces.

00:41:30.808 --> 00:41:35.839
People came from other parts of Spain to see them.

00:41:35.899 --> 00:41:40.694
Many psychic experts were interested too.

00:41:40.754 --> 00:41:49.121
Professor de Argomossa of the University of Madrid started studying the faces.

00:41:49.182 --> 00:41:57.845
He also studied the chemical composition of the floor, but he found nothing unusual.

00:41:57.905 --> 00:42:09.285
Professor de Argomossa discovered that in the 17th century, the Governor of Granada executed five people in Belmes.

00:42:09.345 --> 00:42:16.904
But this was not a complete explanation, because there were more than five faces.

00:42:16.964 --> 00:42:22.456
Workmen started digging under the Pereira's house.

00:42:22.516 --> 00:42:27.540
They found many skeletons under the kitchen floor.

00:42:27.600 --> 00:42:31.281
Two skeletons were headless.

00:42:31.342 --> 00:42:34.884
Was this an old cemetery?

00:42:34.944 --> 00:42:37.306
Yes, it was.

00:42:37.366 --> 00:42:43.470
In the past, there was a cemetery in the same place as the house.

00:42:43.531 --> 00:42:50.243
Perhaps the faces were the spirits of the dead in that cemetery.

00:42:50.304 --> 00:43:03.309
Professor Di Argomossa heard horrible cries and frightened voices in the Pereira kitchen.

00:43:03.369 --> 00:43:07.771
He made a recording of the cries and voices.

00:43:07.831 --> 00:43:12.452
He could also hear words in Spanish.

00:43:12.512 --> 00:43:20.286
Experts from other countries went to Belmas to study the mysterious faces.

00:43:20.346 --> 00:43:27.378
The psychic expert, Jose Martinez Romero, wrote a book about them.

00:43:27.438 --> 00:43:33.544
But no one has an answer, yet.

00:43:33.604 --> 00:43:40.200
Listening exercise, chapter 7.

00:43:40.261 --> 00:43:47.263
Professor D'Argomosa wants to know more about the mysterious faces.

00:43:47.323 --> 00:43:54.946
Listen to this interview between Maria Pereira and Professor D'Argomosa.

00:43:55.005 --> 00:44:03.446
For each question, choose the correct answer, A, B or C.

00:44:03.506 --> 00:44:08.206
When did you see the first face?

00:44:08.266 --> 00:44:11.836
I saw it on Tuesday morning.

00:44:11.896 --> 00:44:14.107
What time was it?

00:44:14.167 --> 00:44:17.417
It was half past seven.

00:44:17.477 --> 00:44:19.868
What were you doing?

00:44:19.928 --> 00:44:24.048
I was preparing breakfast for my family.

00:44:24.108 --> 00:44:28.169
Please describe the face you saw.

00:44:28.229 --> 00:44:33.698
It was a man with black hair and green eyes.

00:44:33.758 --> 00:44:36.448
He was very sad.

00:44:36.508 --> 00:44:38.580
Were you scared?

00:44:38.640 --> 00:44:41.362
Of course I was scared.

00:44:41.422 --> 00:44:44.164
I called my son Miguel.

00:44:44.225 --> 00:44:45.836
Where was he?

00:44:45.896 --> 00:44:49.429
He was working in the vegetable garden.

00:44:49.489 --> 00:44:51.882
What did he do?

00:44:51.942 --> 00:44:56.646
When he saw the face, he called the police.

00:44:56.706 --> 00:44:59.228
What did the police say?

00:44:59.288 --> 00:45:02.610
They told me to call you.

00:45:02.670 --> 00:45:06.432
May I take some photographs of the kitchen floor?

00:45:06.493 --> 00:45:10.716
Yes, of course.

00:45:10.776 --> 00:45:23.780
Chapter 8 Literary Ghosts and the supernatural are part of literature.

00:45:23.840 --> 00:45:28.388
Let's meet some famous literary ghosts.

00:45:28.448 --> 00:45:34.646
William Shakespeare used ghosts in several of his plays.

00:45:34.706 --> 00:45:42.630
In Hamlet, the castle guards see the ghost of Hamlet's father one night.

00:45:42.690 --> 00:45:51.884
Then the ghost speaks to Hamlet and tells him terrible things about his murder.

00:45:51.944 --> 00:46:00.228
Shakespeare's play Macbeth begins with three ugly witches.

00:46:00.288 --> 00:46:08.182
They tell Macbeth and Banquo strange things about their future.

00:46:08.242 --> 00:46:18.870
Later on in the play, Banquo's ghost appears at a banquet table and scares Macbeth.

00:46:18.930 --> 00:46:28.725
In Richard III, the sad ghosts of two boy princes appear to King Richard.

00:46:28.785 --> 00:46:33.546
He murdered them earlier in the play.

00:46:33.606 --> 00:46:43.618
In Julius Caesar, Caesar's ghost appears to remind Brutus of his crime.

00:46:43.678 --> 00:46:56.038
The American writers, Nathaniel Hawthorne and Edgar Allan Poe, were very interested in the supernatural and in spirits.

00:46:56.098 --> 00:47:03.594
Their stories often talk about ghosts, evil spirits and demons.

00:47:03.654 --> 00:47:11.164
In Poe's stories, death and the supernatural are often present.

00:47:11.225 --> 00:47:21.950
In Elinora, 1842, the ghost of Elinora returns to give a message to the narrator.

00:47:22.010 --> 00:47:35.241
In Hawthorne's novel, The House of the Seven Gables, unhappy people and strange spirits live in an evil old house.

00:47:35.302 --> 00:47:50.482
His short story, Young Goodman Brown, 1846, talks about a young man and his adventure in the forest with witches and the devil.

00:47:50.542 --> 00:48:02.316
Charles Dickens' A Christmas Carol, 1843, is a complete ghost story with four ghosts.

00:48:02.377 --> 00:48:13.078
Jacob Marley and the ghosts of Christmas past, Christmas present and Christmas yet to come.

00:48:13.138 --> 00:48:20.340
The ghost of Jacob Marley is an important character of the story.

00:48:20.400 --> 00:48:26.854
Wilkie Collins was a writer and a friend of Charles Dickens.

00:48:26.914 --> 00:48:31.542
He was the father of the modern mystery story.

00:48:31.602 --> 00:48:43.032
He also wrote a complete ghost story called The Haunted Hotel, 1879.

00:48:43.092 --> 00:48:51.394
At the end of the 19th century, the ghost story became a literary form.

00:48:51.454 --> 00:49:03.866
The Cantoville Ghost 1887 by Oscar Wilde is an excellent example of a humorous ghost story.

00:49:03.926 --> 00:49:10.138
The ghost makes friends with one of the characters of the story.

00:49:10.198 --> 00:49:30.248
In The Turn of the Screw, 1898, Henry James created a macabre ghost story about two evil ghosts and their two young victims, a very frightening tale.

